{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.nonroad.model",
    "description": "THE NONROAD DOMAIN MODEL (PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e). One model, no `data_sources`: `../moves-nonroad.esm` mounts it over the national default database and one thin document per RunSpec in `runspecs/nonroad/` mounts THAT and supplies the run's selections and its oracle. It is `fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm`'s model lifted out of the fixture -- the Phase 2 vertical slice, NONROAD's `prccty.f` chain from base-year population through `agedist.f`'s fold to `clcems.f`'s roll-up -- and the fixture stays where it is, because its 29 inline assertions run there and a mounted component's do not (F47).\n\nWHAT THE FIXTURE DECLARED AND THIS DOCUMENT READS. The fixture wrote five things into itself that a document serving more than one run cannot: (1) the six equipment points, `point_sourceTypeID = [1059, 1386..1390]`; (2) the county, state, year and day, as parameters; (3) the base year 1990; (4) the technology window 100..199; (5) the output relation's four pollutants per cohort. Here (1) is `sut_isPoint` -- the `nrsourceusetype` rows whose SCC is in the RunSpec's `/SOURCE CATEGORY/` packet (`scc_isSelected`, with NONROAD's rule that an EMPTY packet runs everything) and whose county population is positive -- ranked densely onto the point axis; (2) comes from `runspeccounty`, `runspecstate`, `runspecyear` and `runspecday`; (3) from `nrbaseyearequippopulation`; (4) is `engineTech`; and (5) is `n_runspecpollutantprocess`. The allocation moved from the point axis to the equipment-type axis, because the surrogate is the equipment type's and the point axis is not known until the allocation is.\n\nWHAT THE SECOND AND THIRD RUNS FOUND, which the first could not. `nr-lawn-garden-county` has SCCs whose exact rate rows cover some technologies and not others, so NONROAD's SCC chain (`fndefc.f`: exact, `xxxxxxx000`, `xxxx000000`) is walked per (pollutant, technology) and not once per point (`tech_rateRow`); and it has points ON a bin boundary -- 37 national points sit on one -- which take the LOWER bin in both the rate and the tech-mix lookups rather than the sum of both (`tech_rate*Row`, `point_mixBinLow`). `nr-recreational-county` selects SO2, which `clcems.f` does not read from a table but WRITES from BSFC and THC, so the rate and deterioration lookups moved onto the axis of what NONROAD always rates (`rated_pp_rows`), and `emsadj.f`'s sulfur correction reads the in-use sulfur of the county's nonroad fuel supply (`fk_sulfurWeightPercent`). `nr-logging-county`'s 144 rows stayed byte-identical to the fixture's through all of that, and left it only at the SEASON file's printed month fractions (PLAN.md §7.3.37), which the fixture does not read. `fixtures/nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county.esm` had found three of these rules first; a fourth it found -- that a (pollutant, technology) pair with no `nrdeterioration` row deteriorates by 1 and not 0 -- is here too.\n\nIT IS EVALUATED IN BINARY32, and the declaration that makes it so is NOT this document's `domain`: the pinned toolchain drops a mounted leaf's `domain.element_type` and evaluates it in the ROOT's precision, silently (docs/findings F60). So every RunSpec in `runspecs/nonroad/` declares `Float32` itself, and `nr-logging-county` without it loses exactly the four rows `docs/nonroad-logging-county.md` §7.3 says binary64 costs. Twenty-one variables still override to Float64, and each holds an SCC or a constant that meets one in the same operator.\n\nFOUR NUMBERS ARE DECLARED, because no table states them and MOVES works them out at run time: `n_equipmentPoint`, `n_outputCohort`, `n_outputPolProcess` and `n_foldYear`. Each is recomputed by the chain -- `run_equipmentPointsSelected`, `run_outputCohortCount`, `run_outputPolProcessCount`, `run_extraScopeRows` -- and tools/check-nonroad-shape.py asserts the declaration against the recomputation and the emitted keys.\n\nSTATE SCALE IS A COUNTY AT A PSEUDO-COUNTY (PLAN.md §7.3.35). MOVES runs a state-level RunSpec at county stateID x 1000, zone stateID x 10000 and fuel region stateID, which it BUILDS (`PreAggSTATE.sql`, `DefaultDataMaker`) and no national table has. So the temperature is a weighted SUM over zones (`zone_runWeight`, divided by the 13 daytime hours and not by the weights, which are rounded before they are divided and sum to less than 1), the nonroad fuel supply is one union relation of the national rows and one default row per `nrFuelType` (`rsu_*`), the `.OPT` packet's func A falls back to formulation 10 when the default formulation 12 joins nothing, and nothing is allocated. At a real county each piece reduces to the formula it replaced. The output carries only what NONROAD EMITS (`emitted_pp_rows`), clamped at zero per record as `NonroadOutputDataLoader` does.\n\nNATION SCALE IS A COUNTY 0 (PLAN.md §7.3.36), and it is NOT a sum of state runs. `PreAggNATION.sql` folds every state into one state 0 before NONROAD sees a table, and the model computes each fold from the national rows (`run_isNationScale`), leaving out Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands as it does (`state_is_in_nation`): the population is the states' SUM, `.POP`-rounded once afterwards (`sut_runPopulation`); the growth pattern is the states' MINIMUM per SCC (`gpf_runStateID`, a `min_sum`); the month allocation is another table, `nrUSMonthAllocation`, so the run's month table is a union (`rma_*`); the temperature is the start-weighted mean over every zone, renormalized where a state's is not; the fuel supply is every region's share weighted by the region's start activity (`sup_regionShare`); and the output has no state. Off the nation each is the formula it replaced.\n\nDIESEL, LPG, CNG AND THE WHOLE INVENTORY (PLAN.md §7.3.37). A RunSpec selecting onroad diesel matches no `nrscc` fuel ID, so its packet is empty and NONROAD runs all 213 SCCs; the dense layout runs that in ~9 minutes and ~5 GB. Five rules came with it, each about where NONROAD applies an operation or what MOVES hands it: the `/PM BASE SULFUR/` packet's per-technology alternates and `clcems.f`'s diesel PM sulfur correction (`tech_pmSulfurBase`, `tech_sulfatePMScale`); every technology set divided by its sum, as `rdtech_moves.f` does (`tech_fraction`, with `run_mixSetsOffOne` keeping the one-bin check); the zero clamp per TECHNOLOGY record, which is what `NonroadOutputDataLoader` reads (`tech_hourlyEmission`); the rate row's hp bin chosen as `fndefc.f` chooses it, the NEAREST (`hp_bin_distance`); and the month fraction as the SEASON file prints it, renormalized (`printed_decimal`). The output's fuel type is `nrscc`'s, unmapped.\n\nNOT CARRIED YET: two residuals of `nr-railroad-support-nation` (`runspecs/nonroad/pending/`) -- gasoline SO2 at the nation 1.38e-4 high throughout, and one diesel cohort -- reformulated gasoline, CO2 and crankcase, and the air-toxics and speciation chain `fixtures/nr-airtoxics-lawn-garden-county.esm` computes."
  },
  "domain": {
    "element_type": "Float32"
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_nrscc": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrscc, discovered by the source's own `extent` (esm-spec §8.9.4). The default is 0 because the count is not knowable until the table is read, and a fixture that hardcoded 214 here would be asserting the snapshot's shape rather than measuring it -- the next snapshot has a different number of rows. A zero that survives to evaluation means the source was never sampled, which is a build error and not a small answer."
    },
    "n_nrequipmenttype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrequipmenttype. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrsourceusetype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrsourceusetype. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrbaseyearequippopulation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrbaseyearequippopulation. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrstatesurrogate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrstatesurrogate. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_runspecmonth": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecmonth. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_runspeccounty": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspeccounty. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecstate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecstate. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecyear": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecyear. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecday": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecday. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecsector": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecsector. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecfueltype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecfueltype. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecpollutantprocess -- the output gate, and the fixture's pollutant axis. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrmonthallocation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrmonthallocation. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrusmonthallocation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrusmonthallocation. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrdayallocation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrdayallocation. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_zone": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in zone. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_zonemonthhour": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in zonemonthhour -- the largest table this fixture reads. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_year": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in year. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_regioncounty": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in regioncounty. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrfuelsupply": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrfuelsupply. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_fuelformulation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in fuelformulation. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrfuelsubtype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrfuelsubtype. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrfueltype": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrfueltype. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_nrgrowthpatternfinder": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrgrowthpatternfinder. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrscrappagecurve": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrscrappagecurve -- 197 breakpoints of the default curve. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc. A zero here would make the step lookup reduce over nothing, which the assertions on the age-2 and age-3 scrappage percents catch."
    },
    "n_nrgrowthindex": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrgrowthindex. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrengtechfraction": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrengtechfraction. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_enginetech": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in engineTech. Runtime-discovered."
    },
    "n_nrsulfuradjustment": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrsulfuradjustment. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nremissionrate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nremissionrate. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_nrdeterioration": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in nrdeterioration. Runtime-discovered; see n_nrscc."
    },
    "n_equipmentPoint": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 6,
      "description": "THE FIRST DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many equipment points -- `nrsourceusetype` rows whose SCC the RunSpec selects and whose county population is positive -- the run has. It sizes the point axis and, times NONROAD's 51 age slots, the cohort grid. No table states it, so it is declared and CHECKED both ways: `run_equipmentPointsSelected` recomputes it and `run_equipmentPointsDropped` counts the points a short axis would lose. 6 is `nr-logging-county`'s value."
    },
    "n_outputCohort": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 36,
      "description": "THE SECOND DECLARED NUMBER: how many (SCC, model year) cohorts reach MOVESOutput. The output relation is that times the run's pollutant-processes -- a RECTANGLE, which every nonroad run here is, because each SCC's rate and deterioration rows cover every selected pollutant. `run_outputCohortCount` recomputes it. 36 is `nr-logging-county`'s value: 3, 29 and 4 model years for its three SCCs."
    },
    "n_outputPolProcess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 4,
      "description": "THE THIRD DECLARED NUMBER: how many of the run's selected pollutant-processes NONROAD emits -- the ones whose pollutant has an output slot this model computes (`emitted_pp_rows`). `nr-pleasure-craft-state` selects seven and emits four. `run_outputPolProcessCount` recomputes it. 4 is `nr-logging-county`'s value."
    },
    "n_foldYear": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 31,
      "description": "How many years `agedist.f`'s fold runs, base year to episode year inclusive: `runYearID - runBaseYearID + 1`, 31 for 1990 to 2020. Every run in the corpus is 2020, so it is declared with that default and checked by `run_extraScopeRows` rather than bound per run."
    }
  },
