          "shape": [
            "default_curve_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The equipment type whose scrappage curve this run reads, 0, as a one-row relation so the restriction is a `join.on` and not a filter (§3). WHAT THIS DOES NOT PORT: scrptime reads the curve for the equipment's OWN NREquipTypeID and falls back to 0 when there is none, and that fallback ladder is not here, because this snapshot's nrscrappagecurve is 197 rows all at type 0 and a ladder over one rung would be untestable. A snapshot carrying per-type curves would need it, and would silently mix curves without it -- which is why the restriction is written as a join on a named type rather than left out."
        },
        "slot_ageID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "age_slot_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1-based equipment age in years, 1 to MXAGYR = 51. Age 1 is the newest cohort. This is the fold's slot axis and is longer than `age_rows`, which carries only the cohorts this SCC actually has."
        },
        "slot_modelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "age_slot_rows"
          ],
          "description": "runYearID - (slot - 1): 2020 in slot 1, back to 1970 in slot 51. The slot axis is the same rectangle for every equipment point; which of its members are POPULATED is what differs, and that is `slot_isPopulated`."
        },
        "point_medianLifeYears": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
