        {
          "_comment": "J11. The .TECH rows the equipment chain, the hp bin, the exhaust process group and the cohort's mix year select, laid out per technology. THE ORDER OF THE `join` CLAUSES BELOW IS A COST DECISION AND NOT A READING ORDER -- docs/esm-conventions.md §25, docs/findings/README.md F17. Only the FIRST clause a binding can resolve DRIVES enumeration; the other three still restrict the admitted set, but as per-leaf equality tests (CONFORMANCE_SPEC §5.5.8, `the others are membership tests on the driven leaves`). This node therefore costs exactly what the first clause's match set admits, and every order gives byte-identical rows. Measured on the whole document, one `esm simulate --time 0` each: engTechID first admits 2,320,704 leaves and runs in 11.5 s; SCC first 5,977,200 and 20.4 s; modelYearID first 24,107,900 and 57.2 s; processGroupID first -- a key with TWO distinct values -- 272,523,600 and 541 s. Do not reorder these for legibility.",
