          "_comment": "J12. The rate table's own equipment chain and hp bin, per equipment point, technology and selected pollutant process. The rate depends on the POINT and not on the cohort -- nremissionrate's modelYearID is 1900 throughout this fixture -- so it is contracted once per point and joined onto the cohorts, which keeps a 55,471-row table off the 306-row axis. THE `x 1 g/(hp*h)` IS A UNIT BOUNDARY (conventions §57 rule 8, §58): nremissionrate.meanBaseRate is ONE column in TWO units -- g/(hp*h) on a pollutant row and lb/(hp*h) on the BSFC carrier 9901 -- so the column carries none, and the unit is re-applied HERE, where the join to rpp_polProcessID has selected which pollutant processes these rows are. It multiplies by 1.0 and moves no number.",
